      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've marked the run anomalous, blamed the instrument and process layer, left the specific cause undetermined and asked for a human to check it.\n\n- **What's wrong:** exhaust O2 settled at about 4–8 ppm after the purge and through the ramp. Since growth started at 2520 s it has risen every reading, reaching 54.5 ppm at 3120 s, and it's still going up.\n- **What's normal:** Ar flow is on its 100 sccm setpoint and temperature is holding at 750 °C, so the rise isn't from low purge flow or a heating fault. Air getting into the tube is the likely explanation.\n- **Why the cause is open:** a seal leak is the most likely cause, but this furnace has no pressure gauge. Tube pressure would tell a leak (pressure normal or low) apart from a blocked exhaust (pressure rising). A leak check or a temporary gauge would settle it.\n- **Why a human:** the growth stage needs the pressure gauge to confirm the atmosphere, and it isn't installed. Oxygen at 750 °C may also damage the sample if the run keeps going.\n- **Science:** the sample hasn't been characterized yet. Because the run was anomalous, any result it gives can't count as evidence about the recipe."
     }
